Add a domain-specific language for defining the signals to generate.
It has variables, assignments, and expressions (with +, -, * and brackets).
Statements that just have an expression with no = define the output signals. So
for example to define a tone in each pol (with different frequencies) and a
correlated noise, you could write something like

```
n = wgn(0.5);
cw(0.5, 234e6) + n;
cw(0.7, 345e6) + n;
```

If you wanted both correlated and uncorrelated noise, you could do something like
```
n = wgn(0.5);
cw(0.5, 234e6) + n + wgn(0.2);
cw(0.7, 345e6) + n + wgn(0.2);
```

White Gaussian Noise (wgn) is not implemented yet.

